  "title": "From freeway to expressway",
  "text": "Between 1963 and 1975, significant portions of US 6, now Highway 14, were moved to a freeway alignment. The last interchange near California City is California City Boulevard, and the road's character changes there. The former routing south of Mojave and the current routing to the north are both still known as Sierra Highway.",
